rgb.photo.v1.9f72efe8-2986-4da8-b946-dcba4ce3ea28	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2018-03-30 08:42:37+00	2020-03-15 18:18:36.062+00	3	6000	3376	#365286	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.9f72efe8-2986-4da8-b946-dcba4ce3ea28/rgb.photo.v1.9f72efe8-2986-4da8-b946-dcba4ce3ea28"}	<p>A random swing-set idling under the moon in Monument Valley.</p>
rgb.photo.v1.ddbb7740-e90f-433d-96f8-183e5ee25bd6	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2019-07-13 23:11:12+00	2020-03-15 18:19:13.094+00	3	5304	7952	#999999	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.ddbb7740-e90f-433d-96f8-183e5ee25bd6/rgb.photo.v1.ddbb7740-e90f-433d-96f8-183e5ee25bd6"}	<p>The moon rising in the Enchantments (and likely Venus to the right).</p><p><br></p><p>Black and white night photos are really cool. I normally try to avoid grain in long-exposures. However, I find grainy black and white photos to be beautiful.</p>
rgb.photo.v1.b5117854-405d-49e6-8ded-4a486f0df263	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2019-06-16 04:09:39+00	2020-03-15 18:19:02.627+00	3	4865	6487	#8aa5c6	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.b5117854-405d-49e6-8ded-4a486f0df263/rgb.photo.v1.b5117854-405d-49e6-8ded-4a486f0df263"}	<p>Climbers snaking their way across the Easton Glacier.</p><p><br></p><p>I love the headlights coupled with the light of the full-moon. To me, this symbolizes the light that shines within us as we cast off into the darkness of climbing at night.</p>
