rgb.photo.v1.f8b2f4da-dc4a-44cd-af27-92f14dcdd6ef	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2019-07-21 09:04:53+00	2020-02-18 01:14:31.46+00	5	1262	1010	#305581	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.f8b2f4da-dc4a-44cd-af27-92f14dcdd6ef/rgb.photo.v1.f8b2f4da-dc4a-44cd-af27-92f14dcdd6ef"}	<p>This photo was taken on the 50th anniversary of the Apollo 13 moonwalk. The moon sank below the horizon as we crested the summit crater of Rainier. I immediately thought of my favorite picture of all-time - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthrise" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">the earthrise</a>.</p><p><br></p><p>As the Apollo 8 careened behind the dark side of the moon, William Anders trained his sights on the horizon to capture Earth beaconing him to return home. Just like the early pioneers, I was scared. I had miles of crevasse fields to navigate before I could breathe again. </p><p><br></p><p>I took supreme comfort in the moon. This was the same object I gazed upon with wonder as a kid. This was the same object my ancestors have been inspired by since Mother Nature brought us into existence. As this beacon of comfort faded, I felt my family walking alongside me.</p>
