rgb.photo.v1.d6a7ba10-c355-4739-91ec-45b2fcb4d374	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2017-07-08 15:21:21+00	2020-02-18 22:12:02.971+00	3	3937	2953	#1f191a	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.d6a7ba10-c355-4739-91ec-45b2fcb4d374/rgb.photo.v1.d6a7ba10-c355-4739-91ec-45b2fcb4d374"}	<p><span style="color: rgb(38, 38, 38);">The day's first sun rays illuminating glaciers on of the East Face of Johannesburg Mt. This photo was taken on the longest day of the summer, right before the solar eclipse in 2017. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color: rgb(38, 38, 38);">The universe way in such sync that summer. Every time there was a full moon, it set exactly opposite from the rising sun. Every time the moon was almost new, it trailed the sun as it set below the horizon.</span></p>
rgb.photo.v1.1abaacce-05db-4f89-893a-0c57274749a0	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2014-09-07 09:22:18+00	2020-02-18 19:34:13.173+00	3	1920	1280	#97c0dc	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.1abaacce-05db-4f89-893a-0c57274749a0/rgb.photo.v1.1abaacce-05db-4f89-893a-0c57274749a0"}	<p>Hidden campgrounds tucked into the hills of Big Sur - Some photos are such powerful triggers for memory. When I look at this photo, I can smell the fresh tinge of grass brought on by the early spring rains.</p>
rgb.photo.v1.89daffa6-6fdf-4833-8ccb-5f083398ecfb	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2016-09-14 06:08:39+00	2020-02-18 22:12:02.853+00	3	4359	2906	#c2c2c2	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.89daffa6-6fdf-4833-8ccb-5f083398ecfb/rgb.photo.v1.89daffa6-6fdf-4833-8ccb-5f083398ecfb"}	<p><em>The moon setting over the scraggy peaks of Glacier National Park</em></p><p><br></p><p>This was the first photo I ever printed. Under he guise of my mom's Costco Card, I got a 30''x20'' matte print with a thin white border. I left out an "<em>yew!!!</em>" when I saw the print come off the press. I was hooked. Seeing my photos blown up three times the size of my computer was jaw-dropping; you really can start to feel the size of these peaks.</p>
rgb.photo.v1.d8f4e414-f19f-4235-ab14-31a3b997f2fd	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2017-08-20 22:19:07+00	2020-03-15 18:18:27.126+00	3	878	878	#fbf4eb	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.d8f4e414-f19f-4235-ab14-31a3b997f2fd/rgb.photo.v1.d8f4e414-f19f-4235-ab14-31a3b997f2fd"}	\N
rgb.photo.v1.de4a17b9-1dda-48a0-be56-8f90c872d2dc	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2017-08-08 06:45:45+00	2020-03-15 18:18:34.811+00	3	6000	4000	#0549d0	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.de4a17b9-1dda-48a0-be56-8f90c872d2dc/rgb.photo.v1.de4a17b9-1dda-48a0-be56-8f90c872d2dc"}	<p>The moon rising over the North Cascades as the sun sets.</p><p><br></p><p>The blues and pinks from that Fuji camera! I love the color produced by the Fuji XT2, my main camera. Sometimes I can't help but crank the vibrancy slider...</p>
rgb.photo.v1.7346e7f2-a9c5-46b0-885b-1d8f14a6c558	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2017-01-14 02:04:06+00	2020-03-15 18:18:33.825+00	3	4205	3154	#c1c4ca	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.7346e7f2-a9c5-46b0-885b-1d8f14a6c558/rgb.photo.v1.7346e7f2-a9c5-46b0-885b-1d8f14a6c558"}	<p>The moon sinking below the canopy of the Quinault Rainforest. This photo was taken on a solo trip to the Enchanted Valley. I always feel calm, yet unsettled when I'm by myself in nature as day transitions to night.</p>
rgb.photo.v1.fd59473b-88df-4e8e-a2d1-7f4a100ba8bc	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2017-11-19 05:48:19+00	2020-03-15 18:18:32.75+00	3	5748	3832	#7f73d5	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.fd59473b-88df-4e8e-a2d1-7f4a100ba8bc/rgb.photo.v1.fd59473b-88df-4e8e-a2d1-7f4a100ba8bc"}	<p>We roared along Indian Creek as the moon neared the horizon. <a href="https://www.mountainproject.com/area/105716979/south-sixshooter" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">South Six Shooter Tower</a> got closer and closer in the distance. With not a minute to spare, we skidded on the side of the road as the sliver of the moon disappeared below the tower.</p>
rgb.photo.v1.e3c41ab4-5e8a-40e3-bc1d-67380cf40f50	rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d	photo	2017-09-08 23:42:05+00	2020-03-15 18:18:39.774+00	3	6000	4000	#2c2c61	{"bucket": "charliemcgrady-media-prod", "suffixes": {"lg": {"jpg": "_lg.jpg", "webp": "_lg.webp"}, "md": {"jpg": "_md.jpg", "webp": "_md.webp"}, "sm": {"jpg": "_sm.jpg", "webp": "_sm.webp"}, "xl": {"jpg": "_xl.jpg", "webp": "_xl.webp"}, "xs": {"jpg": "_xs.jpg", "webp": "_xs.webp"}, "xxl": {"jpg": "_xxl.jpg", "webp": "_xxl.webp"}, "xxs": {"jpg": "_xxs.jpg", "webp": "_xxs.webp"}}, "keyPrefix": "rgb.user.v1.ffb2fde6-fba6-40aa-8bb6-55b23d5d3c1d/rgb.photo.v1.e3c41ab4-5e8a-40e3-bc1d-67380cf40f50/rgb.photo.v1.e3c41ab4-5e8a-40e3-bc1d-67380cf40f50"}	<p>The moon rising above the mosque on Lamu Island, a muslim enclave off the coast of Kenya.</p><p><br></p><p>This was my first night in a muslim-majority neighborhood. I jolted awake at 5am for the first prayer of the day, amplified over the loudspeakers in the minaret of the mosque. Over time, I began to anticipate the prayer. A period reminder of what's important in life.</p>
